#{[17592186543558 :question/problem "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{1}{2}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ If the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}?$"] [17592186543680 :question/problem "If $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x^{2}+(y-2)^{2}\\le 4\\},$ then $\\iint_D 1\\,\\mathrm{d}A=$\n\nChoose the polar setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge 0$ and whose integrand is the given Cartesian integrand multiplied by the Jacobian $r.$"] [17592186543704 :question/problem "If $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+y^{2}\\le 4\\},$ then $\\iint_D 1\\,\\mathrm{d}A=$\n\nChoose the polar setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge 0$ and whose integrand is the given Cartesian integrand multiplied by the Jacobian $r.$"] [17592186543707 :question/problem "If $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+2)^{2}+y^{2}\\le 4\\},$ then $\\iint_D 1\\,\\mathrm{d}A=$\n\nChoose the polar setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge 0$ and whose integrand is the given Cartesian integrand multiplied by the Jacobian $r.$"] [17592186543716 :question/problem "If $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-3)^{2}+y^{2}\\le 9\\},$ then $\\iint_D 1\\,\\mathrm{d}A=$\n\nChoose the polar setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge 0$ and whose integrand is the given Cartesian integrand multiplied by the Jacobian $r.$"] [17592186543720 :question/problem "If $D = \\{(x, y): (x - \\frac{3}{2})^{2} + y^{2} \\le \\frac{9}{4}\\}$, then $∬_(D)(x^{2} - y^{2})dA =$\n\nChoose the polar setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge 0$ and whose integrand is the given Cartesian integrand multiplied by the Jacobian $r.$"] [17592186543721 :question/problem "If $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+(y-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}\\le \\frac{9}{4}\\},$ then ${∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A=$\n\nChoose the polar setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge 0$ and whose integrand is the given Cartesian integrand multiplied by the Jacobian $r.$"] [17592186543726 :question/problem "If $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,